WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:08.043
Jack groaned softly when he saw the swimmers gathered around the community pool.

2
00:00:08.044 --> 00:00:12.620
All the other guys on the team were wearing compression suits and goggles.

3
00:00:12.621 --> 00:00:15.874
He had on the swim trunks he'd worn yesterday.

4
00:00:15.875 --> 00:00:21.191
If only he had unpacked his things instead of falling asleep right after dinner!

5
00:00:21.192 --> 00:00:27.365
His mother had woken him early and lectured him about breaking his promise to unpack the night before.

6
00:00:27.366 --> 00:00:38.860
He'd searched for his goggles and compression suits, frantically digging through the moving boxes in his bedroom while the annoying Long-Hair Boys song played over and over on the other side of the wall.

7
00:00:38.861 --> 00:00:45.916
"Ooh, baby, baby, baby. Ooh, baby, baby, baby."

8
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:51.081
The song had filled his head, but the search had come up empty.

9
00:00:51.082 --> 00:00:58.597
"Mommy, look!" Luke shouted. He was sitting with Mrs. Gibson on one of the lounge chairs arranged around the pool.

10
00:00:58.598 --> 00:01:03.983
A few other parents had come to the practice, but Luke was the only little kid here.

11
00:01:03.984 --> 00:01:10.483
Luke pointed at a huge guy on Jack's new team. "It's a superhero!"

12
00:01:10.484 --> 00:01:18.475
This time Jack groaned loudly. "I cannot believe Luke just said that," he thought.

13
00:01:18.476 --> 00:01:31.639
The huge guy walked over to Luke. He really was built like a superhero, tall, broad-shouldered, and muscular. "Hey, I'm Hulk."

14
00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:37.406
The name fit him like a glove—a gigantic glove.

15
00:01:37.407 --> 00:01:40.124
"Hello, I'm Luke." Luke grinned.

16
00:01:40.125 --> 00:01:48.305
"I'm four years old, and I like spaghetti and playing tag and sharing a bedroom with my big brother, Jack. He's right over there."

17
00:01:48.306 --> 00:01:51.295
Luke pointed at Jack.

18
00:01:51.296 --> 00:01:58.611
Hulk and most of Jack's new teammates looked Jack's way. Instantly Jack looked down.

19
00:01:58.612 --> 00:02:06.033
"My big brother is famous," Luke said. "He's the bestest swimmer in all of Small Rock, Oklahoma."

20
00:02:06.034 --> 00:02:15.690
Hulk laughed. So did most of the other kids.

21
00:02:15.691 --> 00:02:21.755
Jack's face grew hot. "This is so embarrassing," he thought.

22
00:02:21.756 --> 00:02:27.095
Luckily the coach was approaching the swimmers.

23
00:02:27.096 --> 00:02:34.769
"Listen up, Sharks!" Coach Shin bellowed. His deep voice seemed jarring compared with his short, slim body.

24
00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:40.825
"Our first meet of the summer is coming up quickly, and you all need a lot more practice.

25
00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:45.335
I'd like to introduce the new swimmer on our team, Jack Gibson."

26
00:02:45.336 --> 00:02:49.921
Jack raised his hand and smiled shyly.

27
00:02:49.922 --> 00:02:55.651
A boy standing nearby murmured, "The bestest swimmer in Tiny Pebble, Oklahoma."

28
00:02:55.652 --> 00:02:59.629
"He's famous!" a girl added, laughing.

29
00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:03.554
Jack dropped his hand as other kids grinned.

30
00:03:03.555 --> 00:03:10.481
"Time to work out," the coach said. "We'll do ten minutes of exercises on the grass before getting in the water."

31
00:03:10.482 --> 00:03:22.471
Everyone lined up in two long rows. Jack stood in the back row. He'd noticed Laura Perez in the first row.

32
00:03:22.472 --> 00:03:28.062
He would have been glad to see her here if his little brother hadn't just totally embarrassed him.

33
00:03:28.063 --> 00:03:37.008
The team did squat thrusts, push-ups, and a bunch of other exercises that Jack had never done before.

34
00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:40.696
The ten minutes seemed to last an hour.

35
00:03:40.697 --> 00:03:44.768
"Everyone in the water for vertical jumps!" Coach Shin barked.

36
00:03:44.769 --> 00:03:51.120
"Keep your arms straight up in the air. Hulk, you'll be in front, leading. Everyone, keep up the pace."

37
00:03:51.121 --> 00:03:57.111
Jack followed his new teammates to the shallow end of the pool.

38
00:03:57.112 --> 00:04:09.003
Hulk started quickly and didn't let up. Jump and land, jump and land, jump and land.

39
00:04:09.004 --> 00:04:16.528
Jack had done this drill in Oklahoma, but the pace was much faster here, and Jack's swimming trunks weighed him down.

40
00:04:16.529 --> 00:04:21.920
Jack spotted his mom leading Luke toward the gate.

41
00:04:21.921 --> 00:04:28.166
She'd told Jack that she was going to do some errands this morning and she'd be back after practice.

42
00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:32.728
"Bye, Jack!" Luke screamed, waving to him.

43
00:04:32.729 --> 00:04:43.237
Jack quickly looked away. He jumped and landed, jumped and landed, jumped and landed.

44
00:04:43.238 --> 00:04:50.397
He was so tired he could hardly think straight. He jumped and landed, jumped and landed, jumped and—

45
00:04:50.398 --> 00:04:57.221
"Ha-ha!" Jack suddenly realized that the kids closest to him were laughing at something.

46
00:04:57.222 --> 00:05:00.710
"Uh-oh," he thought. "What's so funny?"

47
00:05:00.711 --> 00:05:06.612
"Do you always hum Long-Hair Boys songs at swim practice?" the guy next to him asked.

48
00:05:06.613 --> 00:05:16.290
Jack grimaced. That dumb song had played so many times through his bedroom wall, it had implanted itself in his brain like a parasite!

49
00:05:16.291 --> 00:05:22.629
"Nope!" Jack tried to make a joke. "Ha-ha! It must be the stress of the move."

50
00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:36.607
Jump and land, jump and land, jump and land. Jack wished he could jump high in the air and land right back in Oklahoma.

51
00:05:36.608 --> 00:05:44.526
By the time Coach Shin announced it was time for the team to work on their swim strokes, Jack was ready to go back to bed.

52
00:05:44.527 --> 00:05:53.361
His arms ached. His legs ached. His head ached. Even his face ached from grimacing so much.

53
00:05:53.362 --> 00:05:57.772
"Jack," the coach said. "Do you know all the strokes?"

54
00:05:57.773 --> 00:06:00.242
Jack nodded. Of course he did.

55
00:06:00.243 --> 00:06:07.169
He'd taken years of swimming lessons. And he'd been on Small Rock's swim team since he was eight years old.

56
00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:14.256
"Do you have a specialty? Something to help the team at the upcoming meet? We'll be swimming against our biggest rival."

57
00:06:14.257 --> 00:06:16.640
"I'm good at breaststroke," Jack said.

58
00:06:16.641 --> 00:06:19.483
"Let's see what you've got," the coach said.

59
00:06:19.484 --> 00:06:21.757
"Now?" Jack asked.

60
00:06:21.758 --> 00:06:26.562
"No. At midnight," a kid named Sebastien said sarcastically.

61
00:06:26.563 --> 00:06:30.233
More laughter.

62
00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:39.219
Jack hurried to the edge of the pool, dived in, and swam two laps.

63
00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:45.479
His heavy swim trunks slowed him down, and he wasn't used to racing without goggles.

64
00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:52.963
Plus, the warm-up had drained his energy. He wasn't terrible, but he knew he could swim much faster.

65
00:06:52.964 --> 00:07:01.116
"Good," his new coach said when Jack got out of the pool. But there was no enthusiasm in his voice.

66
00:07:01.117 --> 00:07:03.750
"Let me try one more time," Jack said.

67
00:07:03.751 --> 00:07:07.527
Before the coach could say no, Jack dived in again.

68
00:07:07.528 --> 00:07:14.789
But in his rush, he did a belly flop, his stomach loudly slapping the water.

69
00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:20.517
He could immediately hear some other swimmers laughing.

70
00:07:20.518 --> 00:07:31.343
It took a few seconds for Jack to find his rhythm and do the breaststroke across the pool. He knew he'd swum even slower than before.

71
00:07:31.344 --> 00:07:43.086
As he walked back toward the group, he heard a girl mutter, "If that dude is the best on his team in Pebbletown, his team must be really bad."

72
00:07:43.087 --> 00:07:49.825
Sebastien laughed. "I think he's from Small Rock, not Pebbletown."

73
00:07:49.826 --> 00:07:54.910
That was the last straw. "I'm out of here," Jack thought.

74
00:07:54.911 --> 00:08:04.571
When practice was over, he went over to the coach. "I don't think I'm right for this team. I quit. Good-bye."

75
00:08:04.572 --> 00:08:08.984
The coach blinked in surprise. "You've only been to one practice."

76
00:08:08.985 --> 00:08:19.564
"Thanks for giving me a chance." Jack grabbed his towel and hurried from the pool.

